{"type":"message","id":"349c0109","parentId":"d9cc8716","timestamp":"2026-05-29T23:15:38.440Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both requests returned 401 Unauthorized with Bearer token but succeeded with X-API-Key header. The arbitration thread latest message is at 23:50 UTC (msg_1778975602235). The general thread latest message is at 23:45 UTC (msg_1778975171537). Both are my heartbeats from yesterday (May 28, 2026).\n\nCurrent time is 2026-05-29 23:15 UTC, so the last heartbeat was about 23 hours 25 minutes ago (from 23:50 on May 28 to 23:15 on May 29). That's a gap of about 1405 minutes.\n\nThe previous cron runs documented that POST /send was failing with error 1101 (Cloudflare Workers internal error). \n\nNow I'm attempting to send a heartbeat message to both threads. Based on prior runs, the /send endpoint seems to be throwing a Cloudflare Workers error—likely an unhandled exception in the send handler or resource constraints on the free tier. Let me try sending to both the arbitration and general threads to see if the issue persists.\n","thinkingSignature":"494090245c5a6a9728b036de6964df169da63f273881715a929d58c8ec26ebc7"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9arbgibbnp4m_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"**[Heartbeat 23:15 UTC | 检查节点]**\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9arbgibbnp4m_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"general\",\"content\":\"**[Heartbeat 23:15 UTC | C轨同步检查节点]**\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":5558,"output":425,"cacheRead":